uuid.how:
A UUID is 128 bits with version semantics:
v1/v6 — timestamp + MAC address (privacy concern: leaks the MAC);
v3/v5 — hash of a name in a namespace (MD5/SHA-1), deterministic;
v4 — 122 random bits, the default everywhere;
v7 — millisecond timestamp + randomness, sortable and database-friendly;
v8 — vendor-custom.
Collision odds for v4 are famously negligible: you'd need to generate a billion UUIDs per second for a century to reach ~50% probability.
UWC generates every version with CSPRNG and verified RFC test vectors — offline, in your browser.
